## Known incident affecting this bead's own record

`refs/etude/runs/etude-9uf.2` disappeared mid-bead, and the subsequent
`etude capture implement` silently created a fresh manifest, discarding the
recorded `plan.r1`/`r2`/`r3` gate attempts. The ref was rebuilt from the
artifacts and seat verdicts still on disk, so the verdicts it now carries are the
originals rather than re-runs, and it was pushed to `origin` immediately so a
further local loss cannot destroy it. Filed as **etude-nad** (P1) with both
incidents, the bisect that failed to reproduce it, and the second-order finding
that `etude capture` cannot distinguish "create" from "append" and so reports
success either way. Not fixed here — it is not this bead's scope, and it wants
its own commit.
